Whisper: the built-in search engines are DuckDuckGo, Google, Bing and Wikipedia

What: SearchEngineSelector.fetchEngineConfiguration() keeps only DuckDuckGo, Google,
Bing and Wikipedia (the user's language edition) of the configured engines, in that
order, and makes DuckDuckGo the default in normal and private windows.
Why: Whisper's default search is DuckDuckGo. The rest of Firefox's list is AI answer
engines (Perplexity) and shopping or partner-only engines (eBay, Amazon, ...) that
Whisper does not offer. Engines the user adds stay. Like the partner codes
(0033-search-no-partner-codes.patch), this runs on the packaged configuration and on
every Remote Settings update alike.
---
--- a/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs
@@ -79,6 +79,19 @@
   }
 }
 
+/**
+ * Whisper: the built-in engines Whisper offers, in this order, and the default
+ * (patches/0036-search-engine-list.patch). No AI answer engines and no shopping or
+ * partner-only engines; the user's own engines (OpenSearch, "Add search engine")
+ * are not part of the configuration and stay as the user added them.
+ */
+const WHISPER_ENGINES = [/^ddg$/, /^google$/, /^bing$/, /^wikipedia(-.+)?$/];
+const WHISPER_DEFAULT_ENGINE = "ddg";
+
+function whisperRank(engine) {
+  return WHISPER_ENGINES.findIndex(re => re.test(engine.identifier));
+}
